These scripts load the saved .jls files and extract results to CSV for further analysis. Run reload_session.jl first in a fresh Julia session, then include any of the analysis scripts below.

File	Description
extract_results.jl	Extracts the core shortfall matrix (shortfall_mean.csv), regional LOLE matrix (eventperiod_regionperiod_mean.csv), region names, and PRAS headline metrics (EUE, LOLE, NEUE) to pras_headline_metrics.csv. Run this first before any other analysis script
worst_10_analysis.jl	Identifies the 10 worst shortfall hours ranked by system-level unserved energy. Produces top10_summary.csv (worst hour details), top10_matlab_zone_matrix.csv (zone-level shortfall at each worst hour), top10_structural.csv (structural decomposition), and top10_renewable_profile.csv (VRE availability at worst hours)
capacity_analysis.jl	Computes installed capacity and annual capacity factors by technology and zone. Produces capacity_factor_analysis.csv and capacity_factor_by_zone.csv
event_analysis.jl	Detects and characterises individual shortfall events (consecutive hours with non-zero shortfall) using ShortfallSamples. Produces event_details.csv with duration, magnitude, and start time per event
dr_sensitivity.jl	Sweeps DR volume (2.5–20 GW) and payback window (1, 4, 8, 24 hours) for shift and shed DR types. Re-runs assess() for each configuration and saves results to dr_sensitivity.csv. Run in the no-DR session only
dr_impact_analysis.jl	Compares DR and no-DR scenarios by loading both shortfall_mean.csv files. Computes regional EUE change, H2 SOC by hour of day, battery charging/discharging profiles, and DR utilisation by zone. Requires both DR and no-DR sessions to have run extract_results.jl first
dr_mechanism_proof.jl	Provides quantitative evidence for the DR payback mechanism. Analyses correlation between shortfall worsening and prior-window stress, event structure change, new-zone shortfall timing, and borrowed vs returned load balance
dr_average_day.jl	Computes average-day demand and VRE profiles for the poster figure, and performs the direct vs failed-shifting shortfall decomposition. Produces dr_average_day.csv, dr_best_day.csv, dr_shortfall_decomposition.csv, and dr_decomp_by_hour.csv
dr_sample_case_study.jl	Finds a Monte Carlo sample where DR reduces EUE but increases LOLE, demonstrating the payback mechanism at the individual-sample level
extract_experiment_results.jl	Full extraction script for the sensitivity experiment. Deserialises all results, prints headline metrics and diagnostics to the console, and saves 7 labelled CSVs covering structural deficit hours, interface utilisation, H2 dispatch, battery statistics, and zone EUE

Typical run order for a scenario:

julia
# 1. Fresh Julia session — load variables from saved files
include(raw"path\to\scripts\build\reload_session.jl")

# 2. Extract core results
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\extract_results.jl")

# 3. Run analysis scripts as needed
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\worst_10_analysis.jl")
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\capacity_analysis.jl")
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\event_analysis.jl")

# DR scenarios only:
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\dr_impact_analysis.jl")
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\dr_mechanism_proof.jl")
include(raw"path\to\scripts\analysis\dr_average_day.jl")
